{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>What</b> — he says addressing Doeg: \"Why do you boast in evil, you mighty man, to do evil.\"" "And the meaning of <b>the lovingkindness of El</b> all the day — one should praise only the lovingkindness of El, which encompasses us. Or its meaning is: \"Do you not know that the lovingkindness of YHWH is with me all the day\"? And the proof is that he said at the end: \"I trust in the lovingkindness of Elohim forever and ever.\" And some say: it is defective [missing] a kaf, like כחסד ה' (\"like the lovingkindness of YHWH\")."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 52, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:45.957387066Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}